-- #1111 A-2.5 (#1092): the PRELUDE-RUNG cell -- a wrong -> correct move this unit
-- makes and did NOT claim.  AGENTS.md flags exactly this shape as untested by
-- construction: every pre-existing fixture covered the case that RETURNED
-- something (a diagnostic), so no existing golden could fail on a path that
-- newly returns NOTHING.  This file is the missing positive control.
--
-- This module names no user interface at all.  It calls the PRELUDE's `debug`
-- (core's `Debug`) on an `Int`, for which core has an impl.  The program is well
-- typed; EVERY file in this graph must bucket to zero diagnostics.
--
-- It did not.  A user interface elsewhere in the graph (`pdiface.UDbg`) also
-- declares a method named `debug`; the cross-module method table is keyed by the
-- BARE method name and is last-write-wins; the user interface registers AFTER
-- core.  So the impl obligation for this occurrence was recorded against `UDbg`
-- -- an interface this file never imports and never names -- and a valid program
-- was rejected.  MEASURED first-hand on a cold `make medaka` of e572da09
-- (pre-A-2.5), on this exact directory:
--
--   No impl of UDbg for Int   (at the `debug` occurrence in `main`, below --
--   deliberately quoted WITHOUT a line:col, so a later comment edit here cannot
--   silently falsify it)
--
-- What makes it pass is `preludeMethodEntry`, the LAST rung of
-- `scopedMethodEntry` (compiler/types/typecheck.mdk): the implicit prelude is in
-- scope in every module without a `DUse`, so a module that witnesses no import
-- for a collided name resolves it to core's declaration rather than to whichever
-- user interface happened to register last.
--
-- ⚠️ `exit 1 -> exit 0`, i.e. the severity-INCREASE direction if it is wrong, so
-- the expected value was derived from the language and not read off the tool:
-- `bump 1` is 2, and core's `impl Debug Int` is `debug n = intToString n`, so
-- `debug (bump 1)` is "2" and the program is well typed.  Its mirror -- the same
-- overlay machinery having to KEEP rejecting a genuinely missing impl -- is
-- `method_missing_impl_no_collision` in this same corpus.
import pdbridge.{bump}

main : <IO> Unit
main = putStrLn (debug (bump 1))
